      "q": "8. Two primary cells of emf\u00a0${{E}_{1}}$ and ${{E}_{2}}$\u00a0 are connected to the potentiometer wire $AB$ as shown in the figure if the balancing length for the two combinations of the cells are $250cm$ and $400cm$. Find the ratio of ${{E}_{1}}$ and ${{E}_{2}}$ .",
      "a": "It is known that,$E=kl$\n$\\text{ }{{E}_{1}}-{{E}_{2}}=K\\times 250$ \u00a0 \u2026\u2026$(1)$\n${{E}_{1}}+{{E}_{2}}=K\\times 400$ \u00a0 \u2026\u2026$(2)$\nAdding equations $(1)$ and $(2)$\n$2{{E}_{1}}=250~K+400K$\n$$2{{E}_{1}}=250~K+400$$\n$2{{E}_{1}}=650K$\n${{E}_{1}}=\\frac{650}{2}K$\n${{E}_{1}}=325K$\nSubstituting ${{E}_{1}}=325K$ in equation$(1)$\n$\\text{ 325K}-{{E}_{2}}=K\\times 250$\n${{E}_{2}}=325K-250K$\n${{E}_{2}}=75K$\nDivide ${{E}_{1}}$ and ${{E}_{2}}$\n$$\\Rightarrow \\frac{{{E}_{1}}}{{{E}_{2}}}=\\frac{325K}{75K}$$\n$$\\Rightarrow \\frac{{{E}_{1}}}{{{E}_{2}}}=4.33$$\nThe ratio of ${{E}_{1}}$ and ${{E}_{2}}$ is $4.33$."
